.TH SDL_ASSERT_LEVEL 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_ASSERT_LEVEL \- The level of assertion aggressiveness.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_assert.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_ASSERT_LEVEL SomeNumberBasedOnVariousFactors
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This value changes depending on compiler options and other preprocessor defines\[char46]
.PP
It is currently one of the following values, but future SDL releases might add more:
.PP

\(bu 0: All SDL assertion macros are disabled\[char46]
.PP
\(bu 1: Release settings:
.BR SDL_assert
disabled,
.BR SDL_assert_release
enabled\[char46]
.PP
\(bu 2: Debug settings:
.BR SDL_assert
and
.BR SDL_assert_release
enabled\[char46]
.PP
\(bu 3: Paranoid settings: All SDL assertion macros enabled, including
.BR SDL_assert_paranoid \[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

